  "question": {
    "text": "The population $p(t)$ at time $t$ of a certain mouse species follows the differential equation $\\frac{d p(t)}{d t}=0.5 p(t)-450$. If $p(0)=850$, then the time at which the population becomes zero is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "3k1Kk",
      "text": "$\\log 9$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "jyo1P",
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{2} \\log 18$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "l08Tz",
      "text": "$\\log 18$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "scaOf",
      "text": "$2 \\log 18$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\frac{d p}{d t}=0.5 P-450$\nor, $\\int_{850}^0 \\frac{d p}{P-900}=\\int_0^{\\mathrm{t}} \\frac{\\mathrm{dt}}{2}$\nor, $[\\ln |\\mathrm{P}-900|]_{850}^0=\\frac{\\mathrm{t}}{2}$\nor, $\\frac{t}{2}=\\ln \\left|\\frac{900}{50}\\right|=\\ln |18|$\nor, $t=2 \\ln |18|$",
    "image": null
  },
